  "notes": "Product 0x4075 (codename prince), firmware 1.0.6-80+f5f219b; the owner's unit is the retail “QuietComfort SC” (the QuietComfort Headphones sold with a soft case). Same SDP UUIDs as the QC45 (docs/captures/bose-qc-headphones-bluetoothctl.txt), so the bose row picks it unchanged; BMAP on RFCOMM channel 8 with the same [0.1] init ('1.1.0') and the QC45's [31.3] audio modes. What is new is that its owner set up a custom mode in the Bose app: slot 2, voice prompt 00 0b (Work). When [31.3] reports an index other than 0 or 1, the bridge sends START [31.1] (GetAll) once; every configured custom slot with a name or a voice prompt is offered as custom<index>, named in modeLabels. Slot 3 here is configured but has neither, so it is not offered. Every device frame in this pin is from docs/captures/bose-qc-headphones.txt; the capture switched 0, 1, 2, 3 and back on one socket, 28 s, every frame answered.",
